Hadley
Many thanks for responding. In fact like so many things with R the problem was quite different.  The str() I reported in fact referred to a different object with the same name, as I discovered on rebooting R Studio to install the latest version of ggplot2. The str() now showed the object I’d intended, and evidently it was this object which ggplot picked up too.
I guess this means one needs to check the environment for duplicate names - which hadn’t occurred to me.

All best
Neil

